      "role": "user",
      "content": "Container With Most Water\n\nYou are given an integer array height of length n. There are n vertical lines such that the two endpoints of the i-th line are (i, 0) and (i, height[i]). Find two lines that together with the x-axis form a container holding the most water. Return the maximum amount of water.\n\nExample: height = [1,8,6,2,5,4,8,3,7] -> 49.\nConstraints: 2 <= n <= 10^5.",
      "id": "m-1",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-06T05:06:32.307Z",
      "durationMs": 0
    },
